Why this exists
---------------

The GPL requires that whoever receives the program may redistribute it.
Google Play's terms tell users they may not. Distributing a GPL program
only through Play would therefore fail the licence, which is why GPL
apps are usually published in two places at once.

The condition is the substance of it: the permission is worth nothing
unless the unencumbered copy actually exists. Take the app off GitHub
and leave it on Play, and this paragraph stops applying to the version
that is still there.

